## Interface: 120007, 120100
## Title: Pengyou Games
## Notes: Six raid-downtime minigames with a shared virtual-gold ledger. /pg to start.
## Author: Pengyou
## Version: 1.2.0
## SavedVariables: PengyouGamesDB

# ORDERING RATIONALE
#
# The load order below is for GROUPING AND READABILITY, not for dependency
# resolution. It cannot be for dependency resolution, because the language does
# not give it a chance to be: every file's FILE SCOPE runs during load - and
# file scope here only defines functions and tables on PG and registers init
# callbacks (SPEC 2.9) - while all of the real wiring happens later, inside
# those callbacks, at ADDON_LOADED. By the time any init callback runs, every
# file in this list has already been loaded, so PG.Rolls, PG.QuizData and every
# game module are non-nil in ALL of them regardless of the order they appear in
# here. Reordering this list changes the order the init callbacks run in - and
# therefore the order of PG.Comm.Register, PG.Session.OnChange and
# PG.Safety.RegisterWindow calls - but it cannot make a module invisible to
# another module's init.
#
# So the list reads top-down as layers: core plumbing, then the two data/input
# feeds, then the ledger and the widget kit, then the shipped question bank,
# then the games in launcher order, then the three shells that read all of them.
# The three 1.0.0 game files keep their exact relative order and the three
# 1.1.0 games are appended after them: that IS a behaviour statement (it fixes
# init-callback order), so it is deliberate rather than alphabetical tidying.
#
# The one hard rule about this file is its FIRST LINE: it must be a `##`
# directive, never a bare `#` comment, or 12.0.7 skips every directive in the
# file (SPEC 2.13). That is why this block sits below the directives.

Core.lua
Util.lua
Theme.lua
Comm.lua
Rolls.lua
Ledger.lua
Widgets.lua
Data\QuizData.lua
Games\LootGoblins.lua
Games\PullBook.lua
Games\RockPaperScissors.lua
Games\DeathRoll.lua
Games\Gambler.lua
Games\Quiz.lua
Settings.lua
Rules.lua
Launcher.lua
